{
 "what": "Enhanced coupling, Dolby profile: what Dolby's decoder does to an enhanced coupled channel beyond the amplitude, measured as a black box (round 5, P2)",
 "answer": "Within what was measured, nothing of its own. With amplitudes that are the same in every band, Dolby's decoder makes of an enhanced coupling block what it makes of a standard coupling block with the same coupled coefficients: a stream with one amplitude code a frame and its twin, the same frames with standard coordinates of the same values, decode to the same bytes in dlbac3dec on every carrier tried: the round-4 clip, 10 carriers made for this round from 6 independent sources (counting carriers of one source once), and 2 library streams whose independence from the round-4 clip is not verified, 13 in all; and in 4 further pairs that select channels and patterns (2 selections on 2 carriers; 2 more pairs, reuse every 3, repeat sweeps already counted). Amplitudes that differ from band to band were NOT MEASURED: the twin writes one coordinate a channel, and the injector refuses a twin of anything else. Angle, chaos, the angle interpolation and the transient flag are not read (12 streams, one Dolby decode). The amplitude-dependent decorrelation of round 4 is the decorrelation Dolby's decoder applies to every coupled channel (a X + b D(X), evidence 52), its weight moving with the level the code leaves. The candidate model, the existing experimental rule (--decorrelate) laid over enhanced coupling, fails the promotion criterion on every holdout, so no model is added and the conformance row stays NOT MET",
 "method": [
  "tools/ecpl_amp_sweep.py make/dolby/analyse: the round-4 sweep, written down; on the round-4 clip every stream and decode is the bytes of round 4 and the table is the same cell for cell",
  "eac3-ecpl-inject --plan, with the directives of this round: 'target standard' writes standard coordinates of the value of each enhanced coupling amplitude (every code of table E3.10 is one exactly), 'seed zero' pads every rewritten frame so the dither seed word, the 16 bits that end 18 bits before the end, is zero in both twins; 'band', 'channel', 'rest' and 'amp pattern' select",
  "dlbac3dec out-ch-config=7 (5.1) or 0 (2/0), drc-suppress=true drc-mode=custom-0 drc-cut=0 drc-boost=0 drop-delay=true",
  "tools/ecpl_weights.py: per amplitude code the pair (a, b) of a X + b D(X) and the coherence, D the all-pass learned on the stream",
  "tools/ecpl_promotion.py over the carrier files written by ecpl_amp_sweep.py cells; the candidate model's decode is oadec decode --decorrelate of the standard twin, whose coefficients are those of the sweep bit for bit"
 ],
